<tr data-local-id=3D"797f432f-e47b-4834-b459-8b7dce7d2255">
<td data-local-id=3D"a064f1f9-dcbe-4bc3-b457-f24a398aab8b" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"7580e1438e66">3.6</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"efe40d6f4a9b" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d3953785b982"><strong>As a </strong>member cardholder,</p>
<p local-id=3D"c40199cb441c"><strong>I want to </strong>use my card for in-=
person CAD cash withdrawal transactions at ATMs,</p>
<p local-id=3D"c3085df970d4"><strong>So that </strong>I can successfully wi=
thdraw cash from my account</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"b2f7c266-87f7-4d6e-ac3b-c1d4ae38ff99" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"da5a77b7b3ad">The card shall allow the member to complete wi=
thdrawal transactions via Chip and PIN at all ATMs on the following network=
s - OurNet (Beem), Exchange, Acculink, Interac, and Visa - within ATM withd=
rawal amount limits as defined by Beem</p>
<p local-id=3D"464cb80fa3e3">If the specific ATM used supports multiple net=
works, the transaction will be automatically routed via the most appropriat=
e network, in the following order: (1) OurNet (Beem), (2) Exchange, (3) Acc=
ulink, (4) Interac, (5) Visa</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"ba0608d6-081a-46ec-a31f-ab1b578bf3cb" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"dac187f8ae31"><strong>1 - Happy Path:</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"8c0d2c35ba52"><strong>Given</strong> that the withdrawal amo=
unt does not exceed the ATM withdrawal amount limit, and the member has suf=
ficient funds in their account,</p>
<p local-id=3D"8e8482fbb011"><strong>When</strong> the member presents the =
card at the ATM by inserting the Chip, entering the correct PIN, and select=
ing the account (chq/sav), and enters the amount of funds to withdraw,</p>
<p local-id=3D"122139d3864c"><strong>Then: </strong>the transaction success=
fully completes, cash is dispensed, and the member=E2=80=99s account is deb=
ited for the funds</p>
<hr local-id=3D"304dc91f-37f1-4254-9a6b-fa8cf65519ad">
<p local-id=3D"c8bfed475fcb"><strong>2 - Exceeds ATM Withdrawal Limit:</str=
ong></p>
<p local-id=3D"d64b2c0afa99"><strong>Given</strong> that the withdrawal amo=
unt exceeds the ATM withdrawal amount limit,</p>
<p local-id=3D"4a5d636fcbba"><strong>When</strong> the member presents the =
card at the ATM by inserting the Chip, entering the correct PIN, and select=
ing the account (chq/sav), and enters the amount of funds to withdraw,</p>
<p local-id=3D"c3e0f8f6eed2"><strong>Then: </strong>the transaction is decl=
ined</p>
<hr local-id=3D"06a40b4d-9ac3-465b-8d59-9c9fa2dfbfab">
<p local-id=3D"a311a44c961d"><strong>3 - Exceeds Account Balance:</strong><=
/p>
<p local-id=3D"95253268cc9c"><strong>Given</strong> that the withdrawal amo=
unt exceeds the account balance,</p>
<p local-id=3D"128fa33254a8"><strong>When</strong> the member presents the =
card at the ATM by inserting the Chip, entering the correct PIN, and select=
ing the account (chq/sav), and enters the amount of funds to withdraw,</p>
<p local-id=3D"b032e87c86c6"><strong>Then: </strong>the transaction is decl=
ined</p>
<hr local-id=3D"e2ea503b-e9c3-4b6d-8ebe-9989f6639437">
<p local-id=3D"3f6f0bd1fef4"><strong>4 - Incorrect PIN:</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"dde22e2c5d86"><strong>Given</strong> that the member uses an=
 incorrect PIN,</p>
<p local-id=3D"ce60a2b8e502"><strong>When</strong> the member presents the =
card at the ATM by inserting the Chip and entering the incorrect PIN,</p>
<p local-id=3D"f15fb7303ea8"><strong>Then: </strong>the transaction is decl=
ined</p>
