nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"ad21991c7e84"><strong>1 - Happy Path:</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"011caf73a60a"><strong>Given</strong> that the merchant suppo=
rts pre-authorized transactions, the pre-authorization amount does not exce=
ed the purchase amount limit, and the member has sufficient funds in their =
account,</p>
<p local-id=3D"458a35d04e3a"><strong>When</strong> the member provides thei=
r card details and completes the online merchant checkout process,</p>
<p local-id=3D"e8d1fdb9ea0e"><strong>Then: </strong>the pre-authorization s=
uccessfully completes and a hold for the funds is temporarily placed on the=
 member=E2=80=99s account</p>
<hr local-id=3D"78022550-b05e-4e4b-83dc-8a4161c47b99">
<p local-id=3D"c9116400e4f7"><strong>2 - Hold Released:</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"b19fd649256b"><strong>Given</strong> that the pre-authorizat=
ion has successfully completed and a hold for the funds is temporarily plac=
ed on the member=E2=80=99s account,</p>
<p local-id=3D"7c47f1a43722"><strong>When</strong> the member has subsequen=
tly completed the transaction purchase and the transaction amount has been =
debited from the member=E2=80=99s account,</p>
<p local-id=3D"1b32cb828ad3"><strong>Then </strong>the temporary hold is re=
leased</p>
<hr local-id=3D"75f49005-ccba-4c66-a569-cd202b56de80">
<p local-id=3D"250761104243"><strong>3 - Transaction Cancelled:</strong></p=
>
<p local-id=3D"5bc679cafa7b"><strong>Given </strong>that the that the pre-a=
uthorization has successfully completed and a hold for the funds is tempora=
rily placed on the member=E2=80=99s account,</p>
<p local-id=3D"ad0fdb2a4a23"><strong>When</strong> the transaction is subse=
quently cancelled and no funds are debited from the member=E2=80=99s accoun=
t,</p>
<p local-id=3D"2e92516f92be"><strong>Then</strong> the temporary hold is re=
leased</p>
<hr local-id=3D"31f4acd9-590b-49f8-9a5c-5a3e5280d3fc">
<p local-id=3D"30315e37d60c"><strong>4 - Exceeds Purchase Limit:</strong></=
p>
<p local-id=3D"916c050da771"><strong>Given</strong> that the pre-authorizat=
ion amount exceeds the purchase amount limit,</p>
